# The fuzzer itself is a vendored third-party tool.
# What is worth keeping is age2de.yaml, bench/ and this file.
fuzz.py
__pycache__/

# Throwaway experiment metas: targeted profiles, A/B overrides. Prefix new ones with _.
# _full_shuffle.yaml is the exception: it is the meta the fixed seed set was fuzzed with, and
# bench/README.md cites it, so it is not throwaway.
_*.yaml
!_full_shuffle.yaml

# A fuzz run's output is per-run noise, except the benchmark results stored out of it. The fill
# gate in bench/README.md compares a new run against ones recorded here, so those have to
# survive - a run nobody can read is a run the next ticket has to repeat.
# It is `fuzz_output*/*`, not `fuzz_output*/`: git never descends into an ignored directory, and
# the negations below would never be read. `yamls/` is the fixed seed set those results were
# measured on - without it a stored run cannot be reproduced or compared against, which is how
# the `fuzz_output_lock_items` gate was lost. Everything else a run drops is noise.
fuzz_output*/*
!fuzz_output*/yamls/
!fuzz_output*/replay_*.jsonl
!fuzz_output*/timings*.jsonl
!fuzz_output*/report.json

# A scratch log from one run, not a stored result.
bench/replay_items.log
